  "comment": "Type Mastery (design spec section 30): passive, automatic per-type progression - no level-up card needed. XP is earned just by playing (hitting with a move of that type, killing with it, landing that type's status effect), and each of the 5 levels unlocks ONE more effect that reinforces that type's own 'combat grammar' (Electric = Chain/Paralysis, Fire = Burn, Water = Slow/knockback-adjacent, Grass/Poison = DoT, Fighting = armor break, Ghost = confusion, Ice = freeze/shatter) rather than being a flat, type-agnostic damage-percent slider. Effects reuse the SAME effect.type vocabulary as data/items.json wherever possible (type_damage, status_chance) plus two new ones consumed only by TypeMasterySystem/CombatSystem/GameScene: chain_range_bonus (multiplies a chain move's hop range) and target_status_damage_bonus (bonus damage when the move's own type hits a target already afflicted by the named status - the 'paralyzed target takes more Electric damage' style payoff). Effects are CUMULATIVE: reaching level N keeps every effect unlocked at levels 1..N-1 active too. Any type with no explicit entry below falls back to `default`.",
